# PERMIT DENIED — project contract

One-lot top-down dozer gauntlet. Same strip every run. No meta, no campaign, no second player.

**Title** on the window and title screen: `PERMIT DENIED`. Internal shorthand “Killdozer” stays out of copy.

## Doc authority

- `PERMIT_DENIED.md` owns *what* (fantasy). `PERMIT_DENIED_GO_IMPLEMENTATION.md` owns *how* (numbers, signs, APIs).
- Conflict: design wins on fantasy; the implementation guide wins on numbers and APIs.
- `README.md` is how to run, keys, and show-off tests. `assets/usable/ASSETS.md` is the tile/atlas contract.

## Stack lock

Go 1.25 + Ebitengine **v2.9.x**. Module `permitdenied`. 60 TPS (`ebiten.DefaultTPS`). Logical screen **320×224**; window starts **1280×896**. `Layout` always returns `(320, 224)`.

## Stay on the strip

Tune `internal/game/const.go` before adding a system. A threat that does not change **steering** does not ship.

Keep out of this build: between-run unlocks, a second lot, body boons, locational armor, soft-body / particle debris as collision, chopper rockets, a second dozer, `net/http` / accounts / leaderboards, ECS frameworks, Godot / Raylib / a React wrapper.

Copy verbatim: `THE COUNTY SAID NO.`, `BLADE UP` / `BLADE DOWN`, banners in impl guide §10, deaths `ENGINE COOKED` / `TRACK THROWN` / `COUNTY CLOCK`. Do not write Heemeyer, Granby, manifesto, or wanted stars.

## Done

The five show-off tests in `README.md` are the definition of done. After they hold, stop expanding.
